Ukrainian children are learning the skills of 17th-century Cossack warriors – the communities that played a central role in Ukraine history, known for their military skills and horsemanship. But for these students, it is more than a history lesson. It is a chance to escape the reality of growing up during war. Story by Charlotte Lam.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/218ca4dc-b41a-11f1-899b-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-121041-121212-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/218ca4dc-b41a-11f1-899b-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-121041-121212-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">273a82c8-b41a-11f1-9be6-4f06459a85cc</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:21:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Did Trump really obtain 'permanent control' over Greenland?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/did-trump-really-obtain-permanent-control-over-greenland</link><description>
Danish Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen has described a deal for the US to develop a significant military presence on Greenland, as 'a good agreement'. US President Donald Trump announced the deal on Friday, after he spent months seeking to acquire Greenland, citing threats from Russia and China, and even raised the possibility of military action. Story by Charlotte Hughes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d16ac90-b41a-11f1-a12f-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T000307Z-1543419715-RC2WLNA3UJU3-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-MIGRATION-VISA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d16ac90-b41a-11f1-a12f-0730212ba17f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T000307Z-1543419715-RC2WLNA3UJU3-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-MIGRATION-VISA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a7c6e06-b414-11f1-8de3-fb275c31dbd8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:07:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Germany cuts energy tax to lower petrol prices as Merz faces state key elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-germany-cuts-energy-tax-to-lower-soaring-petrol-prices</link><description>
Germany will cut taxes on gasoline and diesel by about 17 cents a litre from October, the government said Friday. The move comes ahead of state elections in the capital Berlin and the northeastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania where Chancellor Friedrich Merz's conservative Christian Democrats are expected to be soundly defeated.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0960e532-b409-11f1-ae11-9f86e9d8151e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:05:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0321c574-b409-11f1-a939-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T093053Z-2036940640-RC2ZINAAJOGS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-ECONOMY-ENERGY.jpg">© Angelika Warmuth, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain's police launch operation to clear migrants off Ceuta beach</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-police-launch-operation-to-clear-migrants-off-ceuta-beach</link><description>
Police on Friday moved hundreds of migrants from the beaches of Ceuta to a temporary camp in the Spanish enclave's port area. The police operation takes place weeks after a record influx of people into Spain's North African tiny territory. During the transfer, the police struggled to contain crowds jostling to get a place at the new tented site. The policing takes place with the issue of migration centre stage in Spain's political debate. Details by Nicholas Rushworth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73cc7560-b410-11f1-b9a7-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T111329Z-520083964-RC2JLNA3KNDI-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/73cc7560-b410-11f1-b9a7-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T111329Z-520083964-RC2JLNA3KNDI-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b26b6802-b40c-11f1-b11d-c1e3642d6b2e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:57:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France’s Macron warns of Russian ‘hybrid’ attacks, seeks to step up energy defence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-macron-warns-of-russian-hybrid-attacks-seeks-to-step-up-energy-defence</link><description>
Just months before France's presidential election, rising fuel costs due to the wars in Iran and Ukraine have pushed the nation to the verge of crisis. In an attempt to address public anger and energy threats, French President Emmanuel Macron gathered the nation's major party presidential candidates at the presidential palace. But the main takeaway from this meeting was perhaps Macron's warning about Russian "hybrid attacks"... what exactly does he mean and how serious is the threat? Details and analysis by Richard Werly, France and Europe correspondent for Blick.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0eb8d6d6-b40c-11f1-8370-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-090800-091732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0eb8d6d6-b40c-11f1-8370-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-090800-091732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">147ffc84-b40c-11f1-952d-eb991228bdb8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:52:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Princess Diana's iconic 'revenge dress' goes to auction</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/princess-diana-s-iconic-revenge-dress-goes-to-auction</link><description>
As the worldwide release of Diana Spencer’s brother’s book prompts a reaction from King Charles and the British Crown, another piece of Diana's legacy is making headlines – the iconic little black dress, worn by the then Princess of Wales, is going under the hammer. Better known as the "Revenge Dress", it would go on to inspire generations of women.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0160137e-b406-11f1-8f9a-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-100959-101205-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0160137e-b406-11f1-8f9a-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260919-100959-101205-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07125c64-b406-11f1-a249-b17150f714a3</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:57:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US and Denmark reach deal on Greenland, Trump claims 'permanent control' over island</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-deal-on-greenland-trump-claims-permanent-control-over-island</link><description>
Not so long ago, inhabitants of Greenland feared that the US was preparing to invade, after US President Donald Trump repeatedly claimed the US wanted to control the Arctic territory. But Trump now says he has struck a deal with Denmark to give Washington "permanent control" over Greenland's security, while ensuring the territory remains firmly in the hands of Denmark. Denmark and Greenland have both hailed the deal, but its exact terms remain unclear. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Washington, Fraser Jackson.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2eeb8a66-b407-11f1-894d-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T213943Z-633036686-RC2OFNA6L8V8-RTRMADP-3-USA-DENMARK-GREENLAND-TALKS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2eeb8a66-b407-11f1-894d-9f514b90f153/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T213943Z-633036686-RC2OFNA6L8V8-RTRMADP-3-USA-DENMARK-GREENLAND-TALKS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8582cd4-b403-11f1-a180-1ba83d71ed50</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:48:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russia reports cyberattacks as parliamentary vote enters second day</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-ukraine-live-russian-strike-on-apartment-building-in-ukraine-s-sumy-kills-at-least-two</link><description>
Russia said Saturday that its electronic voting system in Moscow had come under “powerful” cyberattacks overnight, as parliamentary elections entered their second day. Russian President Vladimir Putin on Friday accused Ukraine of seeking to “hinder” the vote, a claim Kyiv has not publicly addressed. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/663590c0-b3e9-11f1-b4b5-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T050821Z-493016060-RC25MNAON5D8-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-SUMY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/663590c0-b3e9-11f1-b4b5-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T050821Z-493016060-RC25MNAON5D8-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-SUMY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27515156-b3e8-11f1-9e48-a583040d7b27</guid><pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 05:24:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/663590c0-b3e9-11f1-b4b5-9ff5c3f464d4/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T050821Z-493016060-RC25MNAON5D8-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-SUMY.jpg">© State emergency service of Ukraine via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump says US, Denmark reach deal to expand military presence in Greenland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-greenland-denmark-us-deal-un-general-assembly</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said on Friday he had reached a deal with Denmark to expand the US military presence in Greenland, while respecting Danish and Greenlandic sovereignty. Denmark said the agreement would be signed next week during the UN General Assembly but still requires parliamentary approval.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4b96792-b3ab-11f1-a6fd-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26261748094867.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4b96792-b3ab-11f1-a6fd-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26261748094867.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">198a36e4-b3ae-11f1-a710-ef5eae12db34</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:18:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4b96792-b3ab-11f1-a6fd-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26261748094867.jpg">© Jacquelyn Martin, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Sweden's centre-left leader Andersson tasked with forming government after election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-sweden-s-centre-left-leader-andersson-tasked-with-forming-government-after-election</link><description>
Sweden's parliament speaker on Friday tasked opposition leader Magdalena Andersson with forming a government after an election gave the left-wing bloc a narrow majority, setting the stage for difficult coalition talks. Andersson, a former prime minister, must bridge deep differences between four parties, with the centre party ruling out a government that includes the left in cabinet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40e68e1e-b36c-11f1-b0a0-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T081854Z-1103190166-RC2JLNAQH6AJ-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40e68e1e-b36c-11f1-b0a0-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T081854Z-1103190166-RC2JLNAQH6AJ-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">376ca71c-b374-11f1-9745-f7735b9d1ab1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:01:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40e68e1e-b36c-11f1-b0a0-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-18T081854Z-1103190166-RC2JLNAQH6AJ-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-POLITICS.jpg">© Christine Olsson, via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>We’re ideally placed to chair EU budget negotiations, says Irish Minister of State</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260918-we-re-ideally-placed-to-chair-eu-budget-negotiations-says-irish-minister-of-state</link><description>
Ireland is managing a jam-packed agenda as the current holder of the rotating presidency of the EU. We caught up with the country’s Minister of State for European Affairs, Thomas Byrne, who was in Strasbourg for the 2026 State of the Union speech and debate with EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen. We discussed key points from that address, such as a proposed ban on social media access for children, which Ireland is keen to push forward with during its EU presidency.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef4257bc-b282-11f1-86a5-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/GI-BYRNE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef4257bc-b282-11f1-86a5-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/GI-BYRNE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f15d9d8a-b283-11f1-a98d-171d6308f1c7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:17:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Ursula von der Leyen’s sixth State of the Union speech: A grand sweep, but thin on details?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260918-ursula-von-der-leyen-s-sixth-state-of-the-union-speech-a-grand-sweep-but-thin-on-details</link><description>
In this episode, we debrief one of the key annual events in the EU calendar: the State of the Union speech. It was Ursula von der Leyen’s sixth such address as President of the European Commission, and the second State of the Union speech of her second mandate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59db29c6-b285-11f1-9214-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/XT-070396-0916-France24-Lobby-EM01-EN-PGM.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/59db29c6-b285-11f1-9214-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/XT-070396-0916-France24-Lobby-EM01-EN-PGM.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0fa59d04-b286-11f1-8df4-5f3b635e73df</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:17:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Police move hundreds of migrants still in Ceuta off beaches in Spanish enclave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-police-move-hundreds-of-migrants-still-in-ceuta-off-beaches-in-spanish-enclave</link><description>
Spanish police in Ceuta on Friday morning started moving hundreds of migrants from the beaches of the Spanish enclave to a new tented area. Several thousand migrants remain in Ceuta after tens of thousands of people crossed the border with Morocco in late July. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/836abfca-b345-11f1-a6a9-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C86X4R8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/836abfca-b345-11f1-a6a9-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C86X4R8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7bd2f7de-b343-11f1-8c0a-1560ea7fe23b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:51:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/836abfca-b345-11f1-a6a9-af2d0a26bd49/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C86X4R8.jpg">© Antonio Sempere, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia seizes assets of Swiss food giant Nestle and three French firms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-seizes-assets-of-swiss-food-giant-nestle-and-three-french-firms</link><description>
Russian President Vladimir Putin signed a decree Thursday to take control of the Russian assets of Swiss food giant Nestle and three French groups, citing hostile actions by "unfriendly" countries. France responded by calling on Russia to "reverse this decision".  While most Western companies sold their Russian operations and holdings after Moscow launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine, the Kremlin has since made it difficult for firms to leave the country. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/652a0772-b33c-11f1-b4cf-9f16a64db909/w:1024/p:16x9/000-97249KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/652a0772-b33c-11f1-b4cf-9f16a64db909/w:1024/p:16x9/000-97249KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8bcbe04c-b33e-11f1-85e4-bbc13793bae0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:11:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/652a0772-b33c-11f1-b4cf-9f16a64db909/w:1024/p:16x9/000-97249KE.jpg">© Hector Retamal, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia votes in parliamentary election as war in Ukraine drags on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-votes-in-wartime-parliamentary-election-set-to-secure-the-kremlin-power</link><description>
Polls opened in Russia's Far East on Friday as the country began three days of voting for its parliamentary election, the first since Moscow launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine. The Kremlin's main party, United Russia, is poised to keep its grip on power alongside other parties aligned with President Vladimir Putin, as the only party that criticised the war was removed from the ballot. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a45a676c-b331-11f1-adf4-5570cf9529c5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26261239584740.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a45a676c-b331-11f1-adf4-5570cf9529c5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26261239584740.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b8f7924-b320-11f1-8384-fb875830db52</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 05:38:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a45a676c-b331-11f1-adf4-5570cf9529c5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26261239584740.jpg">© Alexander Zemlianichenk, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia targets Kyiv with new missile attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-live-voting-begins-in-russia-s-parliamentary-elections</link><description>
The ⁠Ukrainian ​capital ​Kyiv again came under fire from ‌Russian ⁠missiles on ​Friday, ‌Mayor ‌Vitali Klitschko ​said, with witnesses confirming they could hear explosions in the capital. Earlier, Moscow struck four Ukrainian cargo vessels in the Black Sea, Russian state media said. The latest attacks unfolded as Russians headed to the polls for the country's first parliamentary election since the start of the war. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9962d05a-b387-11f1-ab00-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T064524Z-1817866211-RC2OKNANE6EH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9962d05a-b387-11f1-ab00-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T064524Z-1817866211-RC2OKNANE6EH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">677d63fc-b30f-11f1-b53e-197fcfeabe16</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 03:16:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9962d05a-b387-11f1-ab00-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T064524Z-1817866211-RC2OKNANE6EH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Gleb Garanich, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Trump says 'major progress' made towards US military base in Poland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-trump-says-major-progress-made-toward-us-military-base-in-poland</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said that Washington and Warsaw were making "major progress" towards establishing a US military base in Poland, potentially giving the United States a permanent military foothold on NATO's eastern flank even as his administration reviews its broader troop presence in Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d252d8-4780-11f1-8bbb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-02T083745Z-1119197471-RC2W0LAB5BIB-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-GERMANY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d252d8-4780-11f1-8bbb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-02T083745Z-1119197471-RC2W0LAB5BIB-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-GERMANY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e01662ae-b2fc-11f1-9a8c-710880e29d62</guid><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 01:04:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7d252d8-4780-11f1-8bbb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-02T083745Z-1119197471-RC2W0LAB5BIB-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-GERMANY.jpg">© Kai Pfaffenbach, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>French police officer arrested over suspected far-right terror plot</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-french-police-officer-arrested-over-suspected-far-right-terror-plot</link><description>
A French police officer who allegedly adheres to a "violent radical far-right ideology" has been arrested on suspicion of plotting attacks against state interests and manufacturing 3D-printed weapons, sources told AFP Thursday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/734d60f4-a19b-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34RN2HF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/734d60f4-a19b-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34RN2HF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a3d3092-b2e7-11f1-a6d3-7f9a841973e3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:29:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/734d60f4-a19b-11f1-ba2b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34RN2HF.jpg">© Lou Benoist, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>The Ceuta effect: how far will Europe's anti-migrant backlash go?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260917-the-ceuta-effect-how-far-will-europe-s-anti-migrant-backlash-go</link><description>
As the United States threatens Europe with more tariffs and eyes Greenland, Russia tests the continent’s resolve over Ukraine and the planet overheats, where do citizens feel the biggest threat is coming from? In her Wednesday state of the Union speech, the European Commission president Ursula von der Leyen went big on manning the borders, suggesting new tools to better deal with migration. This comes against in a context of Ceuta where over two days in July, tens of thousands of mostly Moroccans overran Spain’s North African enclave.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf72f42-b2c1-11f1-b3b4-7922de457103/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T083650Z-1505953259-RC26INA4QD32-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf72f42-b2c1-11f1-b3b4-7922de457103/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T083650Z-1505953259-RC26INA4QD32-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0865d082-b2c1-11f1-ad69-6b9ab73b99dc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:16:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>English village holds symbolic vote to leave UK</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/english-village-holds-symbolic-vote-to-leave-uk</link><description>
A village in Oxfordshire has held a symbolic referendum to leave the United Kingdom in protest against government plans to house up to 1,200 asylum seekers at a nearby military base. While the vote has no legal force, it highlights wider tensions over the UK's asylum policy and migration debate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce9f6e32-b2a5-11f1-b76e-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-153343-153523-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce9f6e32-b2a5-11f1-b76e-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-153343-153523-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d42c4c08-b2a5-11f1-a91e-5182ddc2f54d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:17:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Mbappé draws fire from right wing in France, Spain over Ceuta t-shirt controversy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-real-madrid-s-mbapp%C3%A9-draws-criticism-from-far-right-over-ceuta-t-shirt-controversy</link><description>
Real Madrid's French forward Kylian Mbappé is facing mounting criticism by Spanish and French conservative and far-right politicians for partially obscuring a t-shirt supporting residents of Ceuta, Spain's territory bordering Morocco grappling with a migration crisis. Mbappé said he wore the t-shirt rolled up to show solidarity with "all the immigrants who have lost their lives".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2260510-b2a9-11f1-8156-39eb0f836866</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:10:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg">© Omar Arnau Cerezo, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Carney pushes Canada-EU ties beyond trade</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/carney-pushes-canada-eu-ties-beyond-trade</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney used his address to the European Parliament to signal that Ottawa wants to deepen its partnership with the EU beyond trade, expanding cooperation on energy, AI, space and payment sovereignty, while also seeking to join the Erasmus programme. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating explains how the push reflects Canada's broader strategy to build stronger alliances beyond the United States without seeking to join the EU's single market, even as questions remain over how those ambitions can be turned into concrete action.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31e55368-b2a5-11f1-a3c2-fd76b89f47a3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:52:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden: Andersson's centre left claims narrow win</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-andersson-s-centre-left-claims-narrow-win</link><description>
Sweden's centre-left opposition, led by Magdalena Andersson, is set to defeat the incumbent right-wing bloc by one seat after nearly all votes were counted in Sunday's election. The narrow result means coalition talks are likely to be challenging, with parliament due to begin the government formation process on September 28.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5531ffa-b297-11f1-af34-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-131830-131930-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5531ffa-b297-11f1-af34-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-131830-131930-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aab972c8-b297-11f1-b100-95518b0bca84</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:22:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ireland to boycott 2027 Eurovision contest over Israel’s participation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-ireland-to-boycott-2027-eurovision-over-israel-s-participation</link><description>
Ireland will boycott the 2027 Eurovision Song Contest for the second year over Israel's participation, the country's public broadcaster RTE said Thursday. Ireland was one of five countries along with the Netherlands, Iceland, Slovenia and Spain to skip Eurovision this year in protest over Israel’s inclusion in the contest, citing its ongoing war on Gaza.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e99dae4-b29b-11f1-878d-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26260416490287.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e99dae4-b29b-11f1-878d-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26260416490287.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4e524dc-b292-11f1-a08a-c3fc3a34c0a7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:26:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e99dae4-b29b-11f1-878d-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26260416490287.jpg">© Valentina Petrova, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Sweden's left-wing opposition wins slim majority in country's national election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-sweden-left-wing-opposition-wins-slim-majority-in-country-national-election</link><description>
Sweden's left-wing opposition won a narrow majority in the country's general election after the vote count ended Thursday, but faces laborious negotiations to form a government. The incumbent prime minister, conservative Ulf Kristersson, announced his resignation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c51c978-b28f-11f1-a955-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T220139Z-1787689457-RC2LINAN2WVG-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c51c978-b28f-11f1-a955-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T220139Z-1787689457-RC2LINAN2WVG-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5bdfb55c-b28f-11f1-b358-2f46de5ccff5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:02:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c51c978-b28f-11f1-a955-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-13T220139Z-1787689457-RC2LINAN2WVG-RTRMADP-3-SWEDEN-ELECTION.jpg">© Denis Balibouse, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mark Carney's EU speech highlights Canada's shifting alliances</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-mark-carney-s-eu-speech-highlights-canada-s-shifting-alliances-1</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney addressed the European Parliament as Ottawa and Brussels deepen ties against a backdrop of strained relations with the United States. FRANCE 24's Doug Herbert explains how the speech illustrates a broader shift in alliances, with a message that, until recently, would more likely have been delivered in Washington than Brussels.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fb7a19a-b28a-11f1-b70e-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-120914-121514-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fb7a19a-b28a-11f1-b70e-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-120914-121514-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a47c62f6-b28a-11f1-9a68-51f62954151d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:37:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Canadian PM Mark Carney addresses EU Parliament</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/replay-canadian-pm-mark-carney-addresses-eu-parliament</link><description>
